# L §3.4 example: `input rent_wish: money PLN prices 2026 by cpi`.  "Reading it at law date d gives num PLN =
# value × cpi[d] / cpi[2026], exactly. cpi is keyed by one time index, so cpi[d] reads the key whose period
# holds d, and cpi[2026] the key that is the price year itself".  2 000.00 × 105 / 100 = 2 100 PLN read in
# 2027; read in 2026, 2 000.00 × 100 / 100 = 2 000 PLN (a num PLN, printed grouped, L §2.4).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source s "a source"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input cpi[y in years]: num
input rent_wish: money PLN prices 2026 by cpi

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cpi[2026] = 100
  cpi[2027] = 105
  rent_wish = 2 000.00 PLN

ask q1: rent_wish law 2027-03-01
ask q2: rent_wish law 2026-03-01
=== expect
q1: 2 100 PLN
  law date 2027-03-01, cut 2026-01-01
q2: 2 000 PLN
  law date 2026-03-01, cut 2026-01-01
